Falsifies `system_tests::user::name_resolver_tests::a_std_program_asks_each_badge_in_order_until_one_holds_the_name`.

Architecture: aarch64

The defect: std's `lookup_host` asks only the first resolver badge it holds and takes its answer
as the last word. A program granted several zones could then resolve only names in the zone at
slot 9, and the badges at 22 to 28 would be held for nothing.

Expected to fail: the line `lookup packages.nife.test: 10.0.2.9:7777`, read as `PermissionDenied`
from the badge at slot 9, whose zone is `elsewhere.test`. Replayed 2026-10-19 (UTC) on aarch64:
red with exactly that assertion.

